xposed as a union with a raw unsigned machine word view plus alternative generation-specific bit views, including a generic view, extended and younger-generation common views, and per-revision unique views."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u.uvh_event_occurred0_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u.uvxh_event_occurred0_s"],"text":"The generic view carries only a local bus hard-error indicator in the least significant position with the rest reserved, while the extended common view groups hard-error indicators for local, route, link, graphics and network blocks in the low positions, group-zero async errors for a subset of those blocks above them, and reserves the upper range."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u.uvyh_event_occurred0_s"],"text":"The younger-generation common view divides the whole word into one-bit read-write indicators for hard errors, group-zero async errors and group-one async errors over its expanded block set, followed by shutdown, sixteen local bus interrupts, level-one NMI, stop clock, bidirectional ASIC signals and sequence trigger, leaving only the top two bits reserved."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u.uv5h_event_occurred0_s"],"text":"The routed prefix of the UV5 unique view follows the same ordering as the younger-generation view for hard errors, both async-error groups and the start of the local bus interrupt run through interrupt ten, with every observed indicator marked read-write and positions beyond that point outside the routed range."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED0_QP_HCERR_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED0_QP_HCERR_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED0_QP_HCERR_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED0_QP_HCERR_MASK"],"text":"Each shift and mask pair denotes a one-bit field whose mask has exactly that shifted bit set, so a field is tested by shifting and masking and an update must preserve all other bits."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u.uvh_event_occurred0_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u.uvxh_event_occurred0_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u.uvyh_event_occurred0_s"],"text":"Several views contain reserved ranges and gaps between defined bits, so software must not interpret reserved values as meaningful and must preserve them when modifying defined indicators."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":73,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"90fbc6904033e42000ae762f7e22713ee62f438dcdedfc4bd7328bc76c81714c","prompt_sha256":"4043e50a994f51d59dda30871ea71c86924b3ff716b4a8c2b6b2a236a8711ed4","schema":"lx.extract.v1","sids_read":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED0_QP_HCERR_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED0_QP_HCERR_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u"]}
